WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.140 --> 00:00:33.020
[Music]

00:00:33.370 --> 00:00:36.190
[Parran:] The American people, through their elected representatives in Congress,

00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:39.200
have determined to wage unremitting warfare against cancer.

00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:42.920
This disease has been on the increase in recent years.

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:49.700
It now ranks second among the causes of death. It is no respecter of persons.

00:00:49.740 --> 00:00:58.220
Each of you, wherever you live, whoever you are, must become keenly alive to the peril of cancer.

00:00:58.309 --> 00:01:04.420
In the city, on the farm, rich or poor, everyone is a possible cancer victim.

00:01:12.020 --> 00:01:17.540
[Narrator:] Like millions of other women,
Mary Brown's life revolves around her husband and children,

00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:21.320
her church, her club, and her friends. 

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:30.119
Like millions of other mothers, love for her children is equaled only by her feeling of responsibility for their welfare.

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:37.660
What if anything happened to her, she has everything to live for, yet how long has she to live?

00:01:38.120 --> 00:01:43.160
She feels perfectly healthy, yet is desperately afraid.

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:55.380
She has told no one of her fears, not even her husband, but lurking behind her every act

00:01:55.420 --> 00:02:02.520
is the ceaseless ebb and flow of her unspoken worry...it can't be, it is. It can't be. It is.

00:02:06.780 --> 00:02:10.480
To go on with the ordinary day-by-day duties and engagements 

00:02:10.580 --> 00:02:13.800
with this dread always hanging over her. 

00:02:13.940 --> 00:02:15.980
What else is there to do?

00:02:15.989 --> 00:02:20.820
[On a notepad is written Club Meeting 2:30 Tuesday]

00:02:20.820 --> 00:02:25.730
She decides to hear a noted doctor speak at
the woman's club.

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:32.040
[Speaker:] My subject today is the challenge of cancer. 

00:02:32.180 --> 00:02:40.480
Cancer is a lawless growth of our own body, a rebellion of the tiny cells of which we're all made.

00:02:40.480 --> 00:02:50.140
Each year, in the United States, it destroys nearly three times as many of our people as were killed in the world war.

00:02:51.580 --> 00:02:53.820
That is a challenge.

00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:59.080
There's a great deal yet to be discovered about cancer. 

00:02:59.600 --> 00:03:01.040
That is a challenge.

00:03:01.640 --> 00:03:08.860
But with our present knowledge and means of treating it, at least a third of those who die of cancer

00:03:08.870 --> 00:03:15.190
could be saved if they started treatments early enough.

00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:19.940
Fifty thousand needless deaths a year. 

00:03:20.860 --> 00:03:23.920
That is a challenge. 

00:03:24.440 --> 00:03:33.860
To fight this rebellion of our tissues, organized forces are marching ahead on three vital fronts.

00:03:35.140 --> 00:03:42.140
The first of these is research. Scientific
investigation, step by step, one by one,

00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:50.080
substances in almost infinite variations are being prepared and tested to see if they cause cancer.

00:03:50.769 --> 00:03:58.869
Other substances in equally exhaustive manner are being tested to see if they will cure or help to cure cancer.

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:05.879
Still other tests are continually being made to find means of preventing cancer.

00:04:05.879 --> 00:04:12.860
In much of this research, mice and men are partners. Mice are of a similar to human beings

00:04:12.860 --> 00:04:18.859
in their physical development, but their whole life span is only three years.

00:04:19.620 --> 00:04:26.460
A mouse at the age of one year is as old,
from a medical point of view, as a man of forty.

00:04:26.560 --> 00:04:30.740
A two-year-old mouse is nearly seventy.

00:04:30.750 --> 00:04:35.490
That gives us a shorthand method of studying living cancer. 

00:04:35.540 --> 00:04:39.760
Mice, whose heredity is better known than that of any racehorse, 

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:43.440
are as essential for research as are pure chemicals.

00:04:44.260 --> 00:04:49.380
From such experiments, we may assume it's proven that chronic irritation

00:04:49.440 --> 00:04:51.900
often influences the appearance of cancer. 

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:57.200
The chafing of a jagged tooth, rubbing of a shoe on a mole,

00:04:57.220 --> 00:05:05.860
and other forms of continued irritation, internal or external, should be avoided or corrected.

00:05:06.810 --> 00:05:11.430
The field for cancer research embraces all the fundamental sciences.

00:05:11.620 --> 00:05:16.300
In addition to the army of workers with microscopes in laboratories, for example, 

00:05:16.540 --> 00:05:20.420
are the latest and in some ways the most formidable weapons of science.

00:05:21.160 --> 00:05:28.180
The huge machines for smashing the atom, which are being used in studies of the basic problems of cancer.

00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:33.480
To the research workers, therefore,
we can look for the future treatment of cancer

00:05:33.490 --> 00:05:38.970
and on their findings will depend hundreds
of thousands of lives.

00:05:38.970 --> 00:05:45.250
New weapons for the war against cancer, new
engines for the destruction of malignant cells,

00:05:45.250 --> 00:05:51.020
are being developed and tested before going to the soldiers of the treatment front:

00:05:51.020 --> 00:05:56.340
the physicians and surgeons and radiologists.

00:05:56.340 --> 00:06:03.200
Yet, laboratories are often understaffed, technicians underpaid, 

00:06:03.500 --> 00:06:10.380
and vital research projects carefully planned are not started because of lack of funds.

00:06:11.460 --> 00:06:15.720
Congress has taken a big step forward to cope with this need. 

00:06:15.920 --> 00:06:21.640
The National Institute of Health at Washington, D.C., headed by Dr. L.R. Thompson, 

00:06:21.720 --> 00:06:28.100
includes the National Cancer Institute, one of the finest laboratories in the world.

00:06:28.760 --> 00:06:36.620
In it, under the direction of Dr. Carl Voegtlin, cooperative research is being carried on along many lines.

00:06:37.530 --> 00:06:46.330
Congress also by joint resolution has authorized the President to proclaim one month each year as cancer control month.

00:06:47.349 --> 00:06:47.599
of the United States of America the one hundred
and sixty-fourth." Followed by handwritten

00:06:47.349 --> 00:06:47.599
of the United States of America the one hundred
and sixty-fourth." Followed by handwritten

00:06:47.349 --> 00:06:47.599
signature, Franklin D. Roosevelt.]

00:06:47.349 --> 00:06:53.710
The second vital front is treatment. The three
modern methods of curing cancer, surgery,

00:06:53.440 --> 00:06:59.940
surgery, x-rays, and radium, may be used individually or in combination.

00:06:59.940 --> 00:07:04.260
The kind of treatment depends on the type and location of the cancer.

00:07:04.400 --> 00:07:12.400
Surgical procedure today is an elaborate ritual, with equipment of every sort to protect the patient.

00:07:13.940 --> 00:07:20.639
The powerful and invisible x-rays of a two
hundred and fifty thousand volt machine

00:07:20.639 --> 00:07:24.770
are given off when the current passes through a vacuum.

00:07:24.770 --> 00:07:31.360
The administration of these powerful rays
is not only supervised by trained physicians,

00:07:31.360 --> 00:07:37.460
but the patient's safety is further assured
by automatic controlled features.

00:07:37.720 --> 00:07:44.100
Recently developed million-volt machines have been installed at certain hospitals

00:07:44.220 --> 00:07:50.560
and are being used in experiments in super voltage x-ray treatments.

00:07:50.560 --> 00:07:55.900
The third treatment weapon in the war on cancer is radium, 

00:07:55.940 --> 00:08:01.140
a precious metal costing twenty-five thousand dollars a gram. 

00:08:01.420 --> 00:08:12.500
Now this bottle contains eleven ounces of ordinary sand, an amount equal to all the radium in the United States.

00:08:13.509 --> 00:08:18.729
To protect those who work with it, radium
is stored in special containers,

00:08:18.860 --> 00:08:23.820
whose thick walls prevent its rays from escaping. 

00:08:24.260 --> 00:08:28.260
In treatment, radium may be applied in several different ways.

00:08:28.400 --> 00:08:32.620
For example, it may be loaded into a
so-called applicator.

00:08:32.630 --> 00:08:40.350
The applicator in turn is placed in a ponderous lead conveyor for transfer to the treatment room.

00:08:41.280 --> 00:08:48.380
Or it may be enclosed in a massive bomb
from which its rays are directed and controlled

00:08:48.440 --> 00:08:52.460
at an accurately measured distance from the patient.

00:08:57.120 --> 00:09:03.760
[Music]

00:09:03.920 --> 00:09:11.560
Another way in which radium is used to treat cancer is by means of a gas, which emanates from it.

00:09:11.660 --> 00:09:17.300
This is called radon and it's pumped off by an ingenious method.

00:09:19.290 --> 00:09:26.290
The mercury forces the gas ahead of it and into minute tubes of glass or gold.

00:09:26.900 --> 00:09:31.860
These tubes are fused as they are cut, thus capturing the radon 

00:09:32.040 --> 00:09:39.040
so that it can be implanted in effective form directly in the cancer itself.

00:09:46.420 --> 00:09:54.780
Throughout the country, the three recognized methods of treating cancer—surgery, x-rays, and radium—

00:09:54.800 --> 00:10:00.020
can found in more than three hundred cancer clinics which are approved

00:10:00.020 --> 00:10:05.040
by the rigid standards of the American College of Surgeons.

00:10:05.040 --> 00:10:10.960
The disease is also treated effectively in
some centers without approved clinics.

00:10:11.240 --> 00:10:19.059
Unfortunately, all three methods of treatment are expensive and the equipment required is not found everywhere.

00:10:19.059 --> 00:10:24.839
But steps are being taken to make treatment
facilities available to more of our people.

00:10:25.220 --> 00:10:31.980
Cancer is not contagious. It is no more a
disgrace than a broken ankle.

00:10:32.280 --> 00:10:38.960
Many cases of cancer and of pre-cancerous conditions can be treated by having the patients

00:10:38.970 --> 00:10:44.870
come to a cancer clinic periodically, thus receiving treatment with the least interference

00:10:45.060 --> 00:10:47.680
with their work or other activities.

00:10:48.260 --> 00:10:53.520
It is less dangerous today than it ever has
been to have cancer. 

00:10:53.840 --> 00:11:00.400
Tens of thousands of persons are alive and well years after they have had the disease. 

00:11:00.720 --> 00:11:04.940
Some of these people have formed a cured cancer club.

00:11:05.900 --> 00:11:11.940
Why then, you ask, is not everyone cured? The answer is simple.

00:11:12.100 --> 00:11:22.500
Taken in time, a local cancer is curable. Untreated, it will spread throughout the body and become incurable.

00:11:23.200 --> 00:11:29.180
The best insurance against cancer is a complete physical examination once a year

00:11:29.540 --> 00:11:33.200
and alertness for the cancer danger signals.

00:11:33.940 --> 00:11:35.920
Watch for them.

00:11:38.940 --> 00:11:45.140
Any sore that does not heal, particularly about the tongue, mouth, or lips.

00:11:45.920 --> 00:11:50.000
Persistent hoarseness that lasts longer than two weeks.

00:11:51.720 --> 00:11:57.260
Any persistent lump or thickening, especially in the breast.

00:11:59.100 --> 00:12:06.540
Persistent indigestion developing suddenly in middle life. 

00:12:06.840 --> 00:12:12.360
Any irregular bleeding or discharge from any body opening. 

00:12:14.900 --> 00:12:20.180
Sudden changes in the form or rate of growth of a mole or wart.

00:12:20.820 --> 00:12:26.140
Thus, education is the third big front in the war against cancer. 

00:12:26.440 --> 00:12:32.920
Brilliant young scientists and physicians preparing to go to towns and counties where there are no experts 

00:12:32.920 --> 00:12:40.600
are studying on fellowships granted by the Rockefeller Foundation and by the United States Public Health Service.

00:12:41.080 --> 00:12:46.900
State health departments, and state medical societies too, are doing valuable work

00:12:46.900 --> 00:12:52.620
in providing general physicians with the latest
material on cancer controls.

00:12:52.800 --> 00:12:57.600
Public meetings arranged by leaders in the war against cancer 

00:12:57.660 --> 00:13:01.900
are being held throughout the country under the auspices of the 

00:13:02.080 --> 00:13:06.760
Woman's Field Army of the American Society for the Control of Cancer.

00:13:07.180 --> 00:13:14.200
Through these meetings and by other educational efforts, the truth about cancer is presented

00:13:14.209 --> 00:13:22.229
to the people. And the truth is, cancer is
curable when taken in time.

00:13:23.480 --> 00:13:35.440
To you who say with me, I choose to live, 
I say, remember that early cancer can be cured.

00:13:36.230 --> 00:13:45.750
Don't take a chance with cancer. Don't waste time with worry. Don't delay.

00:13:51.180 --> 00:13:57.020
[Mary Brown:] Do I have cancer? You must know after that examination.

00:13:57.020 --> 00:14:00.110
[Doctor:] We must be very thorough, Mary.

00:14:01.120 --> 00:14:04.240
[Mary Brown:] It's been such a relief to tell
someone what I was afraid of.

00:14:04.360 --> 00:14:06.760
[Doctor:] Well, that's what physicians are
for. 

00:14:06.780 --> 00:14:12.180
So many tragedies occur when people are afraid to even go to the doctor.

00:14:12.180 --> 00:14:15.380
[Mary Brown:] If it hadn't been for that meeting, I never should have had courage to come here.

00:14:15.400 --> 00:14:17.220
[Doctor:] Well, I'm glad you didn't delay.

00:14:17.720 --> 00:14:21.320
It's heartbreaking when people with cancer come to us too late.

00:14:22.820 --> 00:14:25.760
[Mary Brown:] Do I have it, I'm not afraid now.

00:14:25.760 --> 00:14:28.000
[Doctor:] Mary, I can't tell you yet.

00:14:28.480 --> 00:14:33.360
I'm going to ask you to go to the hospital tomorrow and then we'll know.

00:14:33.800 --> 00:14:34.940
[Mary Brown:] I see.

00:14:35.540 --> 00:14:40.760
[Narrator:] Tomorrow finds Mrs. Brown in the hospital where experts from many different

00:14:40.760 --> 00:14:44.610
fields of medicine are helping fight her battle.

00:14:44.610 --> 00:14:50.530
To the nearby laboratory comes a small lump of tissue just removed from Mrs. Brown's breast.

00:14:50.530 --> 00:14:56.390
Is it cancer? Here in this division of intelligence of one of the fronts of the war against cancer,

00:14:56.390 --> 00:14:59.329
the answer will be found.

00:14:59.329 --> 00:15:04.610
For microscopic examination, the tissue is swiftly frozen, so that it can be sliced to

00:15:04.610 --> 00:15:11.610
a thinness of two-thousandths of an inch, stained, washed, and mounted on a slide.

00:15:12.819 --> 00:15:15.799
The final decision rests with the pathologist,

00:15:16.100 --> 00:15:20.800
who through years of training can judge the complicated formation of the cells. 

00:15:20.820 --> 00:15:29.300
Thus in a very brief time after the patient has been given an anesthetic, a diagnosis is made.

00:15:31.120 --> 00:15:37.180
He says carcinoma, cancer. Back to the operating room goes the word. 

00:15:37.280 --> 00:15:42.240
A skilled team of surgeons and nurses swings into action.

00:15:45.360 --> 00:15:52.200
In a little while the patient is ready to
leave the hospital. Mrs. Brown is going home.

00:15:52.200 --> 00:15:58.700
Her cancer was an early one and the prompt operation saved her life.

00:16:01.569 --> 00:16:07.900
In a few weeks, she will return for a course of x-ray treatments, and later will report to her physician

00:16:07.900 --> 00:16:13.980
for regular follow-up examinations, even though there is every reason to believe she has been cured.

00:16:13.980 --> 00:16:19.920
She is another of the thousands who learn each year that early cancer is curable.

00:16:21.020 --> 00:16:25.200
With what grateful sincerity, she enlists
in the Women's Field Army,

00:16:25.260 --> 00:16:29.300
that she may give to others the password, choose to live. 

00:16:29.420 --> 00:16:38.040
Thus playing a part in the work of the American Society for the Control of Cancer, whose director, Dr. C.C. Little, says...

00:16:38.049 --> 00:16:42.669
[Little:] Cancer challenges every man and woman. 

00:16:42.840 --> 00:16:50.420
It is a test of our civilization's ability to organize for health and happiness.

00:16:50.680 --> 00:17:01.700
We must meet this disease with the resolution "I choose to live," and to help others to live. 

00:17:01.700 --> 00:17:08.740
I will fight cancer in my own life and wherever I may meet it.

00:17:09.300 --> 00:17:31.740
[Music]

